<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Extremely slow trade reported.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Extremely slow trade reported.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>- U.S. grain merchandisers in the High Plains said business during the latter half of the week was extremely sluggish.</p>
<p>&quot;Yesterday was the slowest day of the month. I did paperwork all day,&quot; a south-central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, merchandisers said the recent cold temperatures in hard red winter wheat growing regions had probably had little ill effect on the crop.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a concern for market reporters and fund managers, but the crop consultants and farmers out here...aren't too worried,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Most basis bids for HRW wheat were unchanged Friday.  </p>
